**/secrets/*

# `junk/` is scratch and stays untracked — except `machines/services1/junk/`, which is
# deliberately tracked: kept dead fragments, each explaining itself in its own header.
# The alternative was what one of them used to be, an `*.ignore` file inside
# `machines/services1/` that looked exactly like live config and that neither the flake
# nor `git status` could see (AGENTS.md rule 5).
junk/
!machines/services1/junk/
!machines/services1/junk/*
initrd*/
tmp/
result-fd
/result

# The cargo workspace's build output: crates/ is one cargo workspace (see
# crates/Cargo.toml), so cargo writes a single target/ there rather than one per
# crate.  The wasm SPAs are separate workspaces and ignore their own.
/crates/target/

# network-status' SPA is the one frontend built with npm; its dependencies are
# regenerated with `npm install` and never committed.
/crates/network-status/frontend/node_modules/

!.env.sample
*.ignore
ai-resources
notes.txt
config.xml

# The wake-word runtime and models: 22 MB of upstream binaries that are pinned
# fetches in crates/whisper-ws/package.nix now. They used to be committed, and a
# committed byte under here is a byte every evaluation of this flake copies into
# the store — docs/flake-simplification-pass-2026-10-24.md §1. `npm run dev`
# reads them from OWW_DIR instead; the fetch is documented in the README that
# stays vendored next to the engine.
/crates/whisper-ws/web/openwakeword/ort/
/crates/whisper-ws/web/openwakeword/models/
